senses.gloss:
1 अ॑व adv. down, off;
 mostly as pref. in nouns and verbs,
rarely as prep. w. abl.

अ॑वकीर्ण a. who has shed (esp. his sperm);
 scattered,
spread;
 bestrewn, filled with, seized by (—˚).

अवग्रह m. hindrance, impediment;
 separation of padas
and the pause between them (g.).

अवचारण n. application (medic.);
 ˚णीय relating to
the application of (—˚).

अवच्छिन्न a. interrupted, bordered or included by
(—˚);
 defined.

अवतार m. descent, esp. of a deity from heaven,
incarnation, appearance;
 a. ˚रिन्.

अवदार m. breaking, rupture. ˚ण a. breaking through,
tearing;
 n. as subst.

अव॑नि f. bed or course of a river;
 river, stream;
 earth,
ground, place (also ˚नी† f.).

अवने॑जन f. ई the same;
 n. washing, wash water^1.
[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.

अवन्ध्य a. not fruitless or vain;
 successful, happy.
˚पात unerring (of an arrow, lit. whose flight is not vain).

आव॑पन n. throwing or putting down, strewing,
scattering, inserting, capacity;
 (also = f. ˚नी) receptacle, vessel.

अवबद्ध a. tied on, fettered;
 fixed by, sticking in
(—˚);
 hanging on, concerned about (loc.).

अवभास m. splendour, light, manifestation, appearance;
˚क a. illumining, manifesting;
 abstr. ˚त्व n.

अवभासन n. manifestation, appearance;
 enlightening,
illumination.

अवभृथ॑ m. bathing after a sacrifice;
 conclusion,
end.

अव˚भृ॑थ m. bathing after a sacrifice;
 conclusion,
end.

अवम॑ a. lowest, vilest;
 nearest, next;
 latest last.

अ॑वर lower, inferior;
 posterior, following, later,
younger;
 nearer;
 preceding (w. abl.);
 western;
 vile, base, mean;
 —˚ at
least in adj., n. in adv. —f. अवरा after-birth.

अवरज a. low-born, born after (another). m. a Śūdra or
a younger brother;
 f. आ a younger sister.

अवरवर्ण m. a low caste;
 ˚ज m. a Śūdra (cf.
prec.).

अवरोध m. hindrance, oppression, investment, siege,
imprisonment, confinement;
 harem, pl. the females of the h.

अवलम्बन f. ई hanging down;
 hanging, leaning,
depending on;
 n. the same as subst. hold, support.

अवश॑ a. independent, uncontrolled, free;
 unwilling,
reluctant.

अवश्य a. not yielding to another's will;
 ˚— & अवश्यम्
adv. necessarily, by all means.

अवष्टम्भ m. leaning or depending on;
 confidence,
courage.

2 अव॑स् adv. down;
 as prep. down from (abl. or instr.), under
(instr.).

अवसक्थिका f. a kind of wrapper;
 ˚कां कृ tie a
cloth round one's legs or knees.

अवसन्न a. sunk down, impressed, deep;
 brought down,
exhausted, afflicted.

अ॑वसित a. (act.) having stopped, having ceased or
desisted from (abl. or —˚);
 (pass.) finished, settled, determined.

अव॑स्तात् adv. underneath;
 on this side, before;
 prep.
under, west of (gen.).

अवस्तु n. a slight or bad thing;
 nonentity, unreality.
Abstr. ˚त्व n.

अवस्थ॑ m. membrum virile. f. आ॑ (often adj. —˚)
state, condition, situation, circumstance, appearance in court;
 vulva.

अवस्थान n. treading upon;
 staying, abiding;
 position,
situation.

अवस्थित a. standing, posted;
 contained or remaining
in, intent upon (loc. or —˚), keeping on, continuing (instr. of an
abstr. or nom. of a pp.), ready to (dat.);
 fixed, settled, firm, steady,
true;
 (thus) situated or circumstanced.

अवहार्य a. to be restored;
 to be made to restore or to
pay (acc.).

अवान्तर॑ a. included, intermediate (˚रा॑म् adv.
between);
 always another, different.

आवरण a. covering, concealing;
 n. the same as subst. +
shutting, enclosing;
 obstruction, hindrance;
 cover, garment;
 bolt, lock;
guard, protection.

आवर्जित a. bent, inclined, poured down, offered,
presented;
 propitiated, won over.

आवर्त॑ m. turning, winding;
 whirl, vortex (lit. & fig.);
tuft of hair on the top of the head or between the eyebrows.

आव॑र्तन a. turning round (tr. & intr.);
 n. turn,
return.

आवश्यक f. ई necessary, inevitable (n. & ˚ता f.
abstr.);
 ˚कं कृ perform the necessities of nature.

आवाप m. scattering, sowing, mixing, inserting, adding;
receptacle, vessel;
 also = हस्तावाप q.v.
